Dafny now builds against Boogie v3.5.5+review.c5a9f2ef, which fixes the background that a prover sends after a reset that follows a new context, and adds two opt-in options, passed with `--boogie "/cacheUsedTypes /lockFreeExpansion"`, that take work out of setting up a prover for each split without changing what the solver gets (on the standard library with 4 cores, 8.6 to 9.4% less wall time with Z3 4.12.1); a program that uses `--standard-libraries` cannot pass them yet, and by default verification is unchanged
